{title: 608 - Faith Is the Victory}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #608 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 608}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F#m]Encamped along [D/F#]the hills of light,
[D]Ye Christians [A7/E]soldiers, rise,
[F#m]And press the [A7]battle ere the night
[F#m]Shall veil the [D/F#]glowing skies.
[D]Against [A/E]the foe [A7/E]in vales below
[A7]Let all [F#m]our strength be hurled;
[D/A]Faith is the [A]victory, [A7]we know,
[A7]That overcomes [D]the [A/E]world.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G#7]Faith is [Em]the victory!
[A]Faith is [A7]the victory!
[D/A]Oh, glorious [A]victory
[A7/G]That overcomes the world.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F#m]His banner over [D/F#]us in love,
[D]Our sword [A/E]the [A7/E]Word of God;
[F#m]We tread the [A7]road the saints above
[F#m]With shouts of [D/F#]triumph trod.
[D]By faith [A/E]they, [A7/E]like whirlwind's breath,
[A7]Swept on [F#m]o'er ev'ry field;
[D/A]The faith by [A]which they conquered [A7]death
[A7]Is still [D/A]our shining [A/E]shield.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F#m]To him who overcomes [D/F#]the foe
[D]White raiment [A7/E]shall be giv'n;
[F#m]Before the [A7]angels he shall know
[F#m]His name confessed [D/F#]in heav'n.
[D]Then onward [A/E]from [A7/E]the hills of light,
[A7]Our hearts [F#m]with love aflame;
[D/A]We'll vanquish [A]all the hosts [A7]of night,
[A7]In Jesus' [D]conq'ring [A/E]name.
{end_of_verse}
